messages:
mira: Heads-up — hit a weird helm templating bug that made the GPU nodeSelector render as a single string and the autoscaler ignored it.

mira: Quick values excerpt: `gpu.enabled: true` and we pass labels via a helper: `{{ include "common.labels" . }}`

mira: Helper we were using (simplified):
```
{{- define "common.labels" -}}
{{- $labels := dict "app" .Values.app "gpu" .Values.gpu.enabled -}}
{{- range $k,$v := $labels -}}
{{ $k }}={{ $v }},
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
```

mira: That produced this annotation on the pod: `gpu=true,` (a single string), and the kube scheduler/node-affinity logic ended up ignoring it.

alex: Hmm — I think the issue is mixing boolean values into a string join. nodeSelector values must be strings, not JSON booleans. Helm's `dict` + range + plain concatenation will stringify, but sometimes it becomes `true` without quotes and downstream tools treat it as non-string.

sam: Short fixes: either quote the boolean when building the map (`quote .Values.gpu.enabled`) or only emit the key when enabled, e.g.:
```
{{- $labels := dict "app" .Values.app -}}
{{- if .Values.gpu.enabled }}
{{- $_ := set $labels "node.kubernetes.io/gpu" "present" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{ toYaml $labels | nindent 4 }}
```

sam: That produces a proper YAML mapping for labels/nodeSelector so types are preserved. Also avoids creating a comma-delimited single string.

tasha: Also worth updating the values schema to prevent booleans in label fields. Our lint didn't catch it because `values.schema.json` allowed `nodeSelector` to be `object` with any type. Add a `patternProperties` or enforce `additionalProperties` of type string. That'll fail fast in CI.

mira: Good call — I opened a tiny PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/charts/pull/312 (just a draft) that: 1) fixes the helper to use `toYaml` and conditional `set`, 2) tightens the values.schema for `nodeSelector.*` => string, and 3) adds a `helm template` smoke step in the chart-ci to run `kubeval` on rendered output.

deploy-bot: Deploy check: chart-ci/lint failed on staging: E003 nodeSelector value type mismatch (detected by kubeval) — see job 8472.

alex: Nice. One more nit: avoid `quote` on booleans if you actually want "true" as a label value; often we prefer a sentinel like "present" or "gpu-vendor:nvidia" so it's explicit.

mira: Agreed — using "present" now. CI green locally, pushing updated branch. Thanks for the quick ideas :thumbsup: 

tasha: Follow-up: add a tiny unit test to `charts/tests` that renders `values.yaml` with `gpu.enabled=true` and asserts `nodeSelector` contains the expected string. Prevent regressions.

mira: Will do. Closing loop once PR is merged. :rocket:
